  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Fanuc-style post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the move with the rotary words (`fanuc.cps` `traverseZ`, `xyFirst`, `onRapid`). On a machine whose table tilts the work, the X/Y traverse of a 3+2 plane or a cross drill then runs at the pose that the previous program left. The #2987 law reads these operations only at their own pose.\n\n- `first_traverse_posed::posed_kind`: the posed law of #3084 now also reads each kind that carries a `Tilt` (the 3+2 planes) and the cross drill.\n- `table_top` / `table_stays`: when every tilting rotary turns the work, the machine table is read fixed where it stands. When a head tilts, the #2987 table law reads it.\n- **The post's declared order.** `tormach.cps` turns A at the safe Z (`G53 G0 Z`, then `G0 A`) before each section's first X/Y traverse. A post now declares that order with the manifest flag `rotariesBeforeTraverse = true` (`post::dialect::turns_rotaries_first`; the same pattern as `liveTooling` and `wcsRotation`).\n  - `tormach.cps` declares it.\n  - When the setup's post declares it, the posed law does not read the operation (for every posed kind, the #3084 kinds included). The #2987 law reads it at its own pose.\n  - Every other post, a user's script without the flag, and a script that does not load read the strict way.\n- The decision is in `docs/decisions/3100-table-tilt-first-traverse.md`.\n\n## Coordinator decisions (recorded in the decision file)\n\n1. The table is read fixed where it stands, not swept.\n2. A test fixture change in `first_traverse_table.rs`. The test `a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work` sets the WCS origin to zero for `Rig::Work`. It now expects the verdict of the block corner on its sphere (29.584) at 20, and a pass at 30.\n3. The cross drill: the one shipped mill-turn (`millturn.mch`) states only a C along Z. So no shipped mill-turn changes, and there is no end-to-end pin for the cross drill.\n4. The declared capability, not a check of the post's name and not a fixture change. Three conditions:\n   - **Backed by a pin.** `posting_rotaries_first.rs` posts three indexed slots through `tormach.cps`. It asserts, in each section, `G53 G0 Z` then `G0 A` before the first X/Y word. A registry check fails when a new shipped post declares the flag without an order test.\n   - **A user's own script is taken at its word, never silently.** A `File` post that declares the flag puts a note on the path.\n   - **The stamp follows the declaration.** The #3084 word is written only when the posed law reads the operation. So `examples/first-4axis-part.camproj` (Tormach PathPilot) keeps its stamps from main, and this PR does not change it.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `first_traverse_table_tilt`:\n  - `a_3_2_plane_under_the_work_a_turning_table_can_leave_turned_up_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `a_3_2_plane_over_every_pose_of_a_turning_table_passes`\n  - `a_post_that_turns_the_table_first_reads_the_plane_at_its_own_pose`\n  - `a_users_own_post_is_taken_at_its_declared_order_with_a_note` (with the negative: the same script without the flag is held by name)\n- `posting_rotaries_first`:\n  - `only_the_tormach_post_declares_that_it_turns_the_rotaries_first`\n  - `the_tormach_post_turns_a_at_safe_z_before_each_first_xy_traverse`\n- `first_traverse_table`: `a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work` (changed)\n- lib: `the_fixed_table_reads_its_top_in_the_paths_height_scale`\n- `tilt_a180_routes` and `tilt_basis0_edited_file` are unchanged. They were red on the first head, and they pass now.\n\n## Readings (debug)\n\nAll green on head b62078f62:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app`:\n  - `--lib`\n  - `tilt_a180_routes`, `tilt_basis0_edited_file`\n  - `posting_rotaries_first`, `first_traverse_table_tilt`, `first_traverse_table`, `first_traverse_posed`\n  - `first_4axis_part`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `index_swing`, `index_swing_horizontal`, `microarc_test_part`\n  - `tormach_fourth_axis`, `tormach_post`, `tormach_wrapped_a`, `tormach_machines`, `tormach_safe_retract`, `tormach_toolchange_lift`\n  - `golden_cl`, `example_catalog`\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post`:\n  - `--lib`\n  - `explain_tormach`, `script_tormach`, `tormach_no_a_word`, `tormach_rotary_travel`, `tormach_same_tool`, `probe_tormach`\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nGreen on the merged head a4d2ac019 (main merged in): `posting_rotaries_first`, `first_traverse_table_tilt`, `first_traverse_table`, `first_traverse_posed`, `tilt_a180_routes`, `tilt_basis0_edited_file`, `first_4axis_part`.\n\nThe first head also ran the cross-drill and mill-turn suites. This head does not change them.\n\nHeavy lanes: the diff reaches the app heavy lanes. Not run, covered by the cut gate.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The cross drill end to end. No shipped mill-turn states a tilting rotary that turns the work.\n- A user's script that declares the flag and does not keep the order. It is taken at its word, with the note.\n- The full quick gate. Only the binaries listed above were run.\n\nChangelog: The first traverse of a 3+2 plane and of a cross drill, on a machine whose table tilts the work, is now judged through every pose that the previous program can leave, unless the post declares that it turns the rotaries at the safe Z before the X/Y traverse (the Tormach PathPilot post does); a clearance under the work turned up is refused by name.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation).\n\nFixes #3100\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
